A started background service can become cached and frozen while its
UEventObserver waits for kernel events. Netlink events do not wake a
frozen app, leaving the alert slider unresponsive. Mark this system app
persistent so its hardware listener remains runnable.

diff --git a/packages/KeyHandler/AndroidManifest.xml b/packages/KeyHandler/AndroidManifest.xml
index 458ac79..0972812 100644
--- a/packages/KeyHandler/AndroidManifest.xml
+++ b/packages/KeyHandler/AndroidManifest.xml
@@ -27,6 +27,7 @@
     <application
         android:icon="@mipmap/ic_launcher"
         android:label="@string/device_settings_app_name"
+        android:persistent="true"
         android:theme="@style/Theme.SubSettingsBase.Expressive"
         android:defaultToDeviceProtectedStorage="true"
         android:directBootAware="true">
